From: FF7 local performance investigation
Subject: [EXPERIMENT E03] drm/amdgpu: opt-in direct sparse REPLACE with retained synchronization

Based on the supplied E01 tree; apply after 0001-amdgpu-explicit-unmap-e01.patch.
This is a private hardware experiment, not a proposed stable ABI or a proven fix.
It retains implicit unmap dependencies and requests TLB invalidation on the new
mapping instead of submitting a separate clear range. Old PRT references are
retired against the replacement fence. All unsupported cases use the original
clear/map path. Accounted control and treatment submit real job counters.

The E01 explicit-sync flag and DELAY_UPDATE are rejected together with the E03
flags. Ordinary applications do not set either private E03 flag.

